.TH "RPIMONITOR-ALERT.CONF" "5" "Oct 18, 2026" "2.13" "RPi-Monitor"
.SH NAME
rpimonitor-alert.conf \- RPi-Monitor alert configuration
.sp
\fBRPi\-Monitor\fP is able to detect if value exceed a defined value or come back to the normal.
.SH OVERVIEW
.sp
Alert/Cancel are sent only when the state is stable to avoid messages
flooding when limit is about to be exceeded as shown in schema bellow:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
                        send alert
                            ^
 th      th <\-\-\-\-\-\-dh\-\-\-\-\-\->|        th
  _____   __________________|______   _______           send cancel
  |   |   |                       |   |     |              ^
  |   |   |                       |   |     |              |
__|   |___|                       |___|     |______________|_____
     tl                          tl        tl<\-\-\-\-\-dl\-\-\-\-\->
                            |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-|
                                    Alert is raised
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If alert is still active after resend period, alerte is sent again:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
                  send alert                                    resend alert
                      ^                                               ^
    th <\-\-\-\-\-dh\-\-\-\-\-\->|<\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-dr\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\->|
    __________________|_______________________________________________|_____
    |
    |
____|
   tl                 |\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\->
                                    Alert is raised
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH CONFIGURATION
.sp
Each alert is identified by its \fB<alert name>\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.active=<activation condition>
<activation condition> defines the alert pre\-condition. If this formula
returns false, the trigger will not be checked. Default value is 1.
This command could refer to KPI using keyword \fBdata.<kpi name>\fP
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.kpi=<trigger>
\fB<trigger>\fP is defining the formula to evaluate. If formula returns true, the
alert is detected. This command should refer to KPI using keyword \fBdata.<kpi name>\fP
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.maxalertduration=<duration before raise>
The alert will be dectected immediatly but alert raised commande will
be executed only afer a defined \fB<duration before raise>\fP in seconds
(\fBdh\fP in the upper schema)
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.cancelvalidation=<duration before cancel>
As for alert raising, cancellation command will be executed only after
\fB<duration before cancel>\fP seconds (\fBdl\fP in the upper schema)
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.resendperiod=<period>
If alert is still active after \fB<period>\fP seconds, the raise command
will be executed again (\fBdr\fP in the upper schema).
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.raisecommand=<Raise Command>
\fB<Raise Command>\fP is the command to executed when an alert is raised.
This command could refer to KPI using keyword \fBdata.<kpi name>\fP
.TP
.B alert.<alert name>.cancelcommand=<Cancel Command>
\fB<Cancel Command>\fP is the command to executed when an alert is canceled
This command could refer to KPI using keyword \fBdata.<kpi name>\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
